<title>USA: Weirton Steel says strong demand continues.</title>
<headline>Weirton Steel says strong demand continues.</headline>
<dateline>WEIRTON, W.Va. 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Weirton Steel Corp said on Thursday that demand for sheet products and tin mill products remained strong in the first quarter of 1997 and the trend has continued into the second quarter.</p>
<p>The company said the completion of its No.1 blast furnace and a tentative labor agreement will help improve the company's performance while cutting operating costs.</p>
<p>Weirton Steel said it has reached a tentative agreement with the Independent Steelworkers Union's production and maintenance workers and the union's salary workers for a four-and-a-half year labor contract.</p>
<p>A ratification vote will take place in the near future, Weirton said.</p>
